--[[
The entry point.

Everything the command line is lives under `compiler.cli`: the option grammar in
`compiler.cli.spec`, one file per subcommand beside it, and the dispatch that finds
the command and hands it a parsed argument list. What is left here is the two
things a program has to do that a library cannot — read `arg`, and exit with a
status.
]]

os.exit(require("compiler.cli").main(arg))
